WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:06.929
Creating photo-realistic materials for light transport algorithms requires carefully fine-tuning a set of material properties

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:09.660
To achieve a desired artistic effect

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:14.920
This is a lengthy process that involves a trained artist with specialized knowledge

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:20.420
In this work we propose a system that only requires basic image processing knowledge

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:26.200
and enables users without photo-realistic rendering experience to create high quality materials

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:33.720
This is highly desirable as human thinking is inherently visual and not based on physically based material parameters

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:40.600
In our proposed workflow All the user needs to do is apply a few intuitive transforms to a source image

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:47.640
and in the next step our technique produces the closest photo-realistic material that approximates this target image

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:54.454
One of our key observations is that even though this process target image is often not physically achievable

00:00:54.460 --> 00:01:00.000
in many cases a photo-realistic material model can be found that closely matches this image

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:07.220
Our method generates results in less than 30 seconds and works in the presence of poorly edited target images

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:11.940
Like the discoloration of the pedestal or the background of the gold material here

00:01:12.939 --> 00:01:16.349
This technique is especially useful early in the material design

00:01:16.659 --> 00:01:22.529
Process where the artist seeks to rapidly iterate over a variety of possible artistic effects

00:01:23.729 --> 00:01:29.819
We also proposed an extension to predict image sequences with a tight budget of one to two seconds per image

00:01:32.119 --> 00:01:36.979
To achieve this we propose a simple optimization formulation that is able to produce

00:01:37.229 --> 00:01:42.229
Accurate solutions but takes relatively long due to the lack of a useful initial guess

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:48.499
our other main observation is that an approximate solution can also be achieved without an

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:54.979
Optimization step by implementing a simple encoder neural network the main advantage of this method. Is that it?

00:01:55.140 --> 00:02:00.949
produces a solution within a few milliseconds with the drawback that the provided solution is only

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:05.569
Approximate we refer to this as the inversion technique both of these solutions

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:12.319
suffer from drawbacks the optimization approach provides results that resemble the target image but is

00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:18.499
Impracticable due to the fact that it requires too many function evaluations and get stuck in local minima

00:02:18.959 --> 00:02:24.319
Whereas the inversion technique rapidly produces a solution, but is more approximate in nature

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:28.549
We show that the best aspects of these two solutions can be fused together

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:36.649
into a hybrid method that initializes our optimizer with the prediction of the neural network this hybrid method opens up the

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:43.579
Possibility of creating novel materials by stitching together the best aspects of two or more materials

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:53.030
Deleting unwanted features through image in painting contrast enhancement or even fusing together two materials

00:02:56.280 --> 00:03:02.000
These synthesized materials can also be easily inserted into already existing scenes by the user

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:07.600
In this scene we made a material mixture to achieve a richer Nebula effect inside the glass

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:14.390
We also show in the paper that this hybrid method not only gives a head start to the

00:03:14.459 --> 00:03:22.009
Optimizer by endowing it with a useful initial guess but provides strictly higher quality outputs than any of the two previous

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:24.260
solutions on all of our test cases

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:32.149
Furthermore if at most a handful of materials are sought the total modelling times reveal that our technique compares

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:35.720
favorably to previous work on mascara material synthesis

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:43.519
We believe this method will offer an appealing entry point for novices into the world of photorealistic material modeling

00:03:43.769 --> 00:03:45.769
Thank you for your attention

